;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 by the user (written by Claude, from design
;; section 15, the System Services, RMS and LIB$ manuals, the guest runs
;; and the debugger run). Why this is right:
;; - PID (a word under -O2), CWD and NL are exported, global symbols
;;   ("::"); GIVEN and RETURNED are the names given to PocRtl.mar's
;;   routines and the values they give back, 256 bytes each, as RMS and
;;   $TRNLNM take at most 255 characters.
;; - Fill copies a string up to its 0X into GIVEN, with its 0X, and its
;;   length to a VAR INTEGER; FALSE once 255 characters are copied and
;;   more remain. The trap 12 calls after their last RETURN are a
;;   function's end without RETURN, never reached.
;; - GetEnv clears val, then for index 0, 1, ... calls POC_TRNLNM with
;;   GIVEN, its length, the index, RETURNED and 255, until it gives -1;
;;   from the second string on, it appends "," (#44) before each. A word
;;   result is taken from R0's low word (MOVW), as INTEGER is under -O2.
;; - System copies its argument, as a value open array, and returns -1.
;; - Unlink returns 2 when the name does not fit, else POC_ERASE's
;;   status, or 0 when that is odd, a success.
;; - Exit takes code MOD 256, floored (the DIVL3, MULL3, SUBL3 and the
;;   correction of a negative remainder), SHORT to an INTEGER, and calls
;;   POC_HALT, which exits with SS$_NORMAL for 0, else %X10000000 + 8 *
;;   code + 2.
;; - The initializer sets PID from POC_PROCESS_ID's low word, plus 32768
;;   if negative (the ADDW3s), CWD from GetEnv("SYS$DISK") and then
;;   POC_DEFAULT_DIRECTORY's string appended, and NL to LF and 0X.
;; - Since the review of 2026-10-10, MakePath, IsDirectory,
;;   MakeDirectory, pathSeparator and AsDirectory have moved to
;;   Directories (expected-vax-Directories.mar), with POC_PARSE and
;;   POC_CREATE_DIRECTORY; what is left differs only in its line numbers
;;   and labels.
;; - On the guest, PlatformOut prints guest-run.expected under -O2 and
;;   -OC: a search list's two strings come back joined with ","; Unlink
;;   of DOOMED.TMP, with two versions, leaves DOOMED.TMP;1, as section
;;   15 said $ERASE would; Exit(3) gives %X1000001A.
; Platform, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
	.TITLE	PLATFORM
